OL,3,AUK falls silent to mark Armistice Day
OL,4,
OL,5,FThe UK has fallen silent on Armistice
OL,6,FDay, commemorating the end of World War
OL,7,FOne and to remember those who have died
OL,8,Fin conflicts.
OL,10,FA national remembrance service took
OL,11,Fplace at the Cenotaph in London, with a
OL,12,Ftwo-minute silence observed at 11:00
OL,13,Fduring ceremonies across England,
OL,14,FScotland, Wales and Northern Ireland.
OL,16,FDefence Secretary Wes Streeting laid a
OL,17,Fwreath at the Cenotaph, which was also
OL,18,Fattended by senior military figures,
OL,19,Fchildren and cadets.
OL,23,APub: 11-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
